PLACEHOLDER-NOT-A-KEY

This file is a stand-in, not a public key. A build embedding it refuses to
install updates: `sinesync update` exits with "this build has no release
signing key; refusing to install an unverified update".

To make releases verifiable, replace this ENTIRE file with a single line
holding the base64-encoded raw 32-byte Ed25519 public key (44 characters
ending in "="). Delete these notes when you do — the parser reads the whole
file, so leaving them behind produces a malformed-key error rather than a
working build.

The matching private key is never stored here or anywhere else in the repo.
It lives only in the GitHub Actions secret RELEASE_ED25519_PRIVATE_KEY and is
generated outside any agent session, piped straight into the secret without
touching disk.

See release_key.go for how this is embedded, and internal/cli/update.go for
how signatures over checksums.txt are verified.
